18	+// Emits a CSV of price-LEVEL operations (op, side, tick_index, shares) each
19	+// followed by the expected best-of-book outputs and clamp flag, for the VHDL
20	+// testbench to replay and assert against. The oracle here implements exactly
21	+// the level-update rule of cpp/itch/order_book_flat.hpp — ADD accumulates,
22	+// REMOVE clamps at zero (the phantom-depth rule from _remove_level) — and the
23	+// best-of-book scan directions (bid from the HIGH index, ask from the LOW).
24	 //
25	-// TODO(vhdl-1): implement per the plan. Keep the CSV schema in ONE place
26	-// (a header string constant) shared conceptually with flat_book_tb.vhd.
