206	+-- Mirrors cpp/itch/order_book_flat.hpp's LEVEL update rule: ADD/REMOVE shares
207	+-- at (side, tick_index), REMOVE clamps at zero on a true underflow (removing
208	+-- more than the level holds — the phantom-depth rule from _remove_level). Best
209	+-- bid/ask come from a priority scan over the per-side level state: bid from the
210	+-- HIGH index down, ask from the LOW index up (same directions as the C++
211	+-- scans). In hardware this is a parallel priority encoder over an occupancy
212	+-- bitmask — constant cycles at any DEPTH, which is the whole comparison against
213	+-- the software O(range) scan. In functional simulation the unrolled loop stands
214	+-- in for that encoder; every op completes in exactly one clock regardless of
215	+-- DEPTH (the range-independence the DEPTH sweep demonstrates).
216	 --
217	 -- Behaviour at op_index >= DEPTH is undefined-by-contract: the golden-vector
218	 -- generator bounds-checks, matching the C++ book's error-count rejection.
219	---
220	--- TODO(vhdl-2): level arrays + clamp logic (parity on level totals).
221	--- TODO(vhdl-3): occupancy bitmask + priority encoders (bid side encodes
222	---   from the HIGH index, ask from the LOW — same directions as the C++
223	---   scans); DEPTH generic sweep must show constant cycles-per-op.
